==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|u}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*kumpa||wave}}, whence also eg. Hungarian {{m|hu|hab||foam}}. {{etyl|gem|fi}} origin is also possible, compare Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*humpaz}} (whence English {{m|en|hump}}).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[hummock]], [[hillock]] (small natural elevation of earth, generally smaller than {{m|fi|kukkula||hill}}, larger than {{m|fi|kumpare||knoll}}).
# A [[mound]] (small, rounded, artificial elevation of earth).

